## VIII. Florida Standards Alignment

Mindful Learning Academy courses are designed to align with Florida academic expectations, including Florida’s B.E.S.T. Standards for English Language Arts and Mathematics where applicable. Course content is structured to support mastery, academic progression, college readiness, and measurable student growth.

---

## IX. Assessment and College Readiness Alignment

Mindful Learning Academy uses a mastery-based instructional model supported by internal and external measures of student progress.

Internal assessment includes:

- Notebook evidence
- Lesson checkpoints
- Lesson quizzes
- Unit assessments
- Performance-based tasks
- Project-based learning artifacts
- Revision cycles based on instructor feedback

External academic progress is measured through a nationally norm-referenced assessment selected by the academy for scholarship compliance, growth monitoring, and instructional planning. Assessment results are used to support placement, academic advising, intervention, enrichment, and parent reporting.

SAT readiness is embedded within English and mathematics coursework. English courses build reading comprehension, vocabulary-in-context, grammar, evidence-based reasoning, and written communication skills. Mathematics courses build fluency in algebra, geometry, data analysis, quantitative reasoning, and problem-solving.

---

## X. Mastery-Based Credit Structure

High school credit is awarded based on demonstrated mastery rather than seat time. Courses are structured around clear learning outcomes, performance expectations, and completion criteria.

Credit is earned through:

- Demonstrated mastery of 80% or higher
- Performance-based tasks and assessments
- Project-based learning artifacts
- Structured feedback and revision cycles
- Weekly goals and pacing expectations
- Time-on-task requirements aligned to course rigor
- Completion of required course components and assessments

